\newlabel{fig:rational_2cycle}{{10}{26}{Basin portrait of $f(z)=(z^2-1)/(z^2+1)$, the simplest proper rational map with a superattracting $2$-cycle $\{0,-1\}$. Degree $d=2$, two critical points ($z=0$ and $z=\infty $), both attracted to the cycle. Chart~1 (left): the two immediate basins $B^0_0$ (orange) and $B^0_{-1}$ (blue) separated by the Julia set. Chart~2 (right): the neighbourhood of $\infty $, which lies in $B^0_0$ since $\infty \to 1\to 0$}{figure.10}{}}
